# Expression construction regressions, not optimization benefit claims.
# Predicate-form Exists is a SemiJoin alias; zero-slot Exists is not.
SemiJoin<p0 a0 a1>(Input<t0>,Input<t1>)|Exists<Not(Not(p0)) a2 a3>(Input<t2>,Input<t3>)|t2 := t0;t3 := t1;a2 := a0;a3 := a1
Exists<p0 a0 a1>(Input<t0>,Input<t1>)|SemiJoin<Not(Not(p0)) a2 a3>(Input<t2>,Input<t3>)|t2 := t0;t3 := t1;a2 := a0;a3 := a1
# FormalSQL certifies the complete predicate under native outer-join semantics.
LeftJoin<p0 a0 a1>(Input<t0>,Input<t1>)|LeftJoin<Not(Not(p0)) a2 a3>(Input<t2>,Input<t3>)|TableEq(t2,t0);TableEq(t3,t1);AttrsEq(a2,a0);AttrsEq(a3,a1)
FullJoin<p0 a0 a1>(Input<t0>,Input<t1>)|FullJoin<Not(Not(p0)) a2 a3>(Input<t2>,Input<t3>)|TableEq(t2,t0);TableEq(t3,t1);AttrsEq(a2,a0);AttrsEq(a3,a1)
